        "Abstract": "We introduce SEAHORSE, a new dataset for evaluating faithfulness in summarization. SEAHORSE consists of 16K human annotations for quality, attribution, and informativeness of summaries generated by different models. We show that SEAHORSE is a challenging benchmark for evaluating summarization models and that it can be used to identify models that are more faithful to the source document."
